      "text": "shepherd is an abomination unto the Egyptians, Gen. 46:34. If a man also lie with mankind, … both of them have committed an abomination, Lev. 20:13. learn to do after the abominations of those nations, Deut. 18:9. all that do unrighteously, are an abomination, Deut. 25:16. according to all the abominations of the nations, 1 Kgs. 14:24. These six things … yea, seven are an abomination unto him, Prov. 6:16. speak truth; and wickedness is an abomination to my lips, Prov. 8:7. Lying lips are abomination to the Lord, Prov. 12:22. way of the wicked is an abomination unto the Lord, Prov. 15:9. thoughts of the wicked are an abomination to the Lord, Prov. 15:26. sacrifice of the wicked is abomination, Prov. 21:27. He that turneth away … even his prayer shall be abomination, Prov. 28:9. ye are … of nought: an abomination is he that chooseth you, Isa. 41:24. their soul delighteth in their abominations, Isa. 66:3. will recompense upon thee all thine abominations, Ezek. 7:3. Go in, and behold the wicked abominations that they do here, Ezek. 8:9. they shall take away … all the abominations thereof, Ezek. 11:18. thou hast multiplied thine abominations more, Ezek. 16:51. hath done all these abominations; he shall surely die, Ezek. 18:13. most desolate because of all their abominations, Ezek. 33:29. place the abomination that maketh desolate, Dan. 11:31 (12:11). their abominations were according as they loved, Hosea 9:10.",
